 ('Someone cuts in line at the coffee shop. You', ['Say "no worries!" and replay it in your head for six hours.', 'Tap their shoulder and announce it to the whole cafe.', 'Smile, let them go, and quietly note which barista likes you better.', 'Order second, tip better, and let them wonder why they feel small.'], ['Six hours of replay and the line cutter forgot your face in six seconds.', 'You gave a stranger a speech and the whole cafe a show. Nobody tipped you.', 'Subtle and petty in the good way. You kept the grudge but skipped the tip.', 'Quiet and lethal. You did nothing and everything.'], 'Violence is loud. Tipping better is permanent. The barista will remember you in March. The line cutter will remember nothing and feel strangely small anyway.'),
 ('Your friend is forty minutes late and texts "omw!!" You', ['Apologize for being early.', 'Send a screenshot of the clock and three knife emojis.', 'Reply "no rush!!" and start a group chat without her.', "Order the appetizer, eat it slowly, and greet her like it's seven o'clock."], ['You apologized for being on time. She is still not sorry.', 'Three knives for a latte date. She read it as flattery and will be later next time.', 'Cold and tidy. You were too busy plotting to taste the appetizer.', 'Appetizer, cool eyes, perfect timing. Nobody was harmed and everyone knew.'], 'Anger is a gift to the late. Calm is a gift to yourself. Eating the appetizer slowly proves the clock was never your problem.'),
 ('A coworker presents your idea as their own. You', ['Tell your cat all about it later.', 'Slam the door so hard it echoes in HR.', 'Compliment them warmly, then forward the original email to the whole team "for context."', 'Say "Glad you like it. Here are the next three steps," and hand out the steps.'], ['The cat agrees with you. The cat has no say in promotions.', 'Doors are not evidence. HR loves a slam and writes the memo about you.', 'Surgical, and the CC list is a work of art. One more step and you would be crowned.', 'Management by menu. She did it cheerfully.'], 'Shouting makes you the story. Handing out the next three steps makes you the manager. Credit is a rental. Leadership is a deed.'),
