 ('Your ex texts "hey stranger" at one in the morning. You', ['Reply "Missed you too!"', 'Write four paragraphs, delete them, write them again.', 'Reply in four seconds: "Who is this?" You saved the number as DO NOT.', 'Leave it unread until Thursday, then send "Just saw this. Hope you\'re well."'], ['Missed you too, said the phone, to the wrong person.', 'Drafts are not a personality. Four paragraphs and he still reads interest.', 'Four seconds. He knows you were awake. So do you.', 'Thursday is a power move. You were never in a hurry.'], 'Instant replies are a leash. Thursday is a verdict. "Hope you\'re well" is the most polite door ever slammed.'),
 ('The waiter brings the wrong dish. You', ["Eat it. It's fine. It's probably fine.", 'Send it back with a note about your disappointment and his tip.', 'Photograph it for a review before he leaves the table.', 'Say "I ordered the other one," pleasantly, once, and wait.'], ["It's fine. The waiter agrees. The chef is now sure his dish is a hit.", 'A note about his tip is a hostage letter. He will not forget the soup either.', 'The review was written before the soup cooled. Somewhere a manager sweats.', 'Pleasant once and patient always. The right plate arrived before you blinked.'], 'One pleasant sentence beats a review. She asked once, she waited, the right plate arrived. Dessert is on him.'),
 ('Someone invites you to a "quick call" that could have been an email. You', ['Say yes, join early, and bring snacks.', 'Reply all with a six paragraph critique of calendars.', 'Accept, mute yourself, and fold laundry.', 'Say "Happy to, send an agenda." No agenda arrives. You never join.'], ['Snacks for the meeting that eats your day. You are why it lasted an hour.', 'Six paragraphs on calendars. One coworker calls you a hero and one has muted you.', 'The laundry gets folded and the meeting goes on. You are the quiet winner of an ugly game.', 'A boundary in business casual. No agenda arrived and you did not miss it.'], 'A request for an agenda is a boundary dressed as help. The silence that follows is the actual answer.'),
